            <ArticleTitle>Unusual presentation of a distal cholangiocarcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1052-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.415</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 51-year-old male presented with abdominal pain and itching, whereas jaundice occurred afterwards. Diagnosis was made by means of CT and better assessed by MRI and endoscopic ultrasounds. Patient was treated with an open Whipple's procedure, and after an 18-month follow-up he was doing well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
